# LOAD-BEARING SAVE FIXTURES — md5 manifest
#
# ‼‼ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. On 2026-08-11 the SAME hazard cost three separate results in one day:
#   1. the `#24-teachmsgstall` "cheap repro" stopped reproducing — `magma_door.ss1` had been
#      re-captured by a `magmatravel` success hours after the failures were measured on it;
#   2. KI-50 was written up as "the chapter wins 1 in 3" — a RATE — when all three losing runs
#      were byte-identical and the single win had been on different bytes of the same filename;
#   3. the KI-52 live A/B was VOIDED — the fixture was pinned *after* a still-in-flight background
#      job had overwritten it, and only the copy was md5'd, never compared to the failing run's.
# Every one of them is "same name, different bytes". Resolving to be careful did not work; this
# file plus `verify_fixtures.py` makes the check mechanical.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#   PYTHONUTF8=1 py -3.12 verify_fixtures.py            # before trusting any fixture-based result
#   PYTHONUTF8=1 py -3.12 verify_fixtures.py --update    # ONLY when you intend a fixture to change
#
# ‼ A save that any DRIVER re-captures is a CACHE, not a fixture. `magma_door.ss1` is rewritten by
# `--driver magmatravel` on every success and `magma_1f_fail.ss1` by `--driver magmahideout` on
# every failure — they are listed as VOLATILE and are expected to drift. Anything you need to hold
# still must be copied to a name nothing writes to.
#
# format:  <md5>  <filename>  <VOLATILE|PINNED>  <what it is / what it is for>

19399688e7302dfe820a2cdbcf04ff1f  post_maxie.ss1  PINNED  §Ch16 build anchor. Post-Maxie era: SLATEPORT_HARBOR_STATE=1, GROUDON_AWAKENED set, Aqua Hideout blocking flags still UNSET. Verified by probe_ch16_anchor.py (all controls green). 59,053 bytes because it came from a profile states/ snapshot, not emulator.get_save_state() — that is a serialisation difference, NOT truncation.
80602159694bf6e95ca0e698481a4cc9  post_mtpyre.ss1  PINNED  Ch15 build anchor. Badges 1-6, Magma Emblem held, MT_PYRE_STATE=1. The start of the Magma Hideout travel leg.
76ef84a3e70c831de06dbe26569d271e  magma_door_losing.ss1  PINNED  DETERMINISTIC boss-loss fixture: reaches Maxie and loses the identical fight every replay (41 turn lines, md5 07f99a10ac8b). Crobat Confuse Ray + Maxie healing Camerupt 22→67. The right fixture for boss-response work.
273d19b34d96733ddda1dee7e7704378  magma_door_ki52.ss1  PINNED  A magma_door save that WINS the chapter (groudon=True, whiteouts=0). ‼ It is NOT the save that produced the KI-52 wedge — that one (8171734228f3) was lost before it could be pinned. Kept because a reliably-winning door save is scarce.
a00378595409bc1b20d40def8d61b846  post_dive_ki76.ss1  PINNED  A PINNED COPY of `post_dive.ss1`, taken 2026-08-17 for `#24-ki76correctness`'s live confirmation. ‼ IT EXISTS BECAUSE `post_dive.ss1` IS VOLATILE — `--driver spacecenter` re-captures it on every PASS (`story_harness.py:3846-3849`, gated by `CH19C_CAPTURE`, default ON). A Tier 2 cold-start audit reported post_dive.ss1 as merely 'not pinned' and I nearly PINNED it; that would have made this gate permanently red the next time anyone ran ch19c. ⛔ The manifest's own rule decides it: a save any DRIVER re-captures is a CACHE, so the fix is a COPY under a name nothing writes to, exactly as post_harbor/post_aqua say.

# --- VOLATILE: expected to change; never base a measurement on these without copying first ---
273d19b34d96733ddda1dee7e7704378  magma_door.ss1  VOLATILE  re-captured by `--driver magmatravel` on every success
275d332a3eb64f195be600bc5c585d8d  magma_1f_fail.ss1  VOLATILE  re-captured by `--driver magmahideout` on every failure. ‼ MISNAMED: it stands on MAGMA_HIDEOUT_4F (24,91), not 1F.
32adff78b86bd4e261e31b6abd407836  post_harbor.ss1  VOLATILE  re-captured by `--driver slateporttheft` on every PASS. Post-Ch16 era: SLATEPORT_HARBOR_STATE=2, standing SLATEPORT_CITY_HARBOR (8,13), 6 badges, party 534/534 HP (healthy BY DESIGN since the heal stops landed, not by accidental whiteout). The build anchor for the NEXT chapter (Lilycove Aqua Hideout) — copy it to a name nothing writes to before measuring on it.
60588e960d13aa4fa44ac1a21a97c83e  post_aqua.ss1  VOLATILE  re-captured by `--driver aquahideout` on every PASS. Post-Ch17 era: TEAM_AQUA_ESCAPED_IN_SUBMARINE set, standing AQUA_HIDEOUT_B2F (24,19), and ‼ a MASTER BALL + Nugget in the bag. The build anchor for the NEXT beat (the Seafloor Cavern) — copy it to a name nothing writes to before measuring on it.
1d38af994837ab54a07dac11423985b5  in_mossdeep_gym.ss1  VOLATILE  re-captured by `--driver mossdeeptravel` on every PASS. Standing MOSSDEEP_CITY_GYM (6,34-35), post-Ch17 era. ‼ Its POINT is that the GYM IS THE LOADED MAP: map_path blocks any tile whose object template is not in active_objects, so reconning this 36-object gym from any other anchor turns all 21 statue tiles into pessimistic walls (KI-58).
a00378595409bc1b20d40def8d61b846  post_dive.ss1  VOLATILE  re-captured by `--driver spacecenter` on every PASS (`story_harness.py:3846-3849`). Post-§Ch19 era: HM08 DIVE in the bag, standing outside in MOSSDEEP_CITY with a real path to the Pokemon Center. ‼ It is the most-used anchor in the project (12+ probes and every `ch20*` driver default to it) and was UNLISTED here until 2026-08-17, so nothing noticed if it moved. ⛔ Copy it to a name nothing writes to BEFORE measuring on it — `post_dive_ki76.ss1` is such a copy.
de5a3aee125338118b2f60d71d06fa42  post_ch20.ss1  PINNED  THE §Ch21 START FIXTURE, captured 2026-08-24 by `--driver ch20chapter` with `CH20_CAPTURE=post_ch20.ss1`. Probe-verified `OVERWORLD ROUTE128 (38,24)`, badges 1-7, `ROUTE128_STATE=2`, `SOOTOPOLIS_CITY_STATE=1` — i.e. Ch21's entry condition, measured live. ‼ PINNED, NOT VOLATILE, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS DELIBERATE: unlike `post_dive.ss1` (which `--driver spacecenter` re-captures on EVERY pass, default ON), this capture is OFF unless `CH20_CAPTURE` is set AND it REFUSES to overwrite an existing file without `CAPTURE_FORCE=1`. So the manifest's "a save any driver re-captures is a CACHE" rule does not apply — nothing writes here by accident. ⚠ Its party has 1 FAINTED member at 80% HP (the honest post-cavern state): heal before a journey, and do NOT read an early whiteout as a Ch21 bug.
862caedfdef52bccbc9ce461a127a2f1  post_sootopolis_arrival.ss1  PINNED  THE §Ch21 LEG-2 FIXTURE, captured 2026-08-24 by `--driver ch21dive` with `CH21_CAPTURE`. Probe-verified `OVERWORLD SOOTOPOLIS_CITY (29,53)`, badges 1-7, `SOOTOPOLIS_CITY_STATE=2` (the arrival cutscene has FINISHED), player SURFING on Deep Water. ‼ CAPTURED ON `arrived`, NOT ON FULL ACCEPTANCE, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE: the run that produced it printed `ACCEPTANCE: FAIL` on a CONTINUATION check that was later proven WRONG (it demanded a walkable path to the Cave of Origin, which Emerald never provides -- Steven's escort warps you in). Refusing to capture until an unrelated check passed would have denied leg 2 its fixture. ⚠ 1 FAINTED party member at 54% HP -- the honest post-arrival state; heal before using it as a start point.
30eefb17b18df134cccfb7f54b5f9f87  post_steven_escort.ss1  PINNED  THE §Ch21 LEG-2b SEAM FIXTURE, captured 2026-08-27 by `--driver ch21escort` with CH21_CAPTURE on FULL ACCEPTANCE. Probe-verified (probe_anchor_inventory): OVERWORLD CAVE_OF_ORIGIN_ENTRANCE (9,20), badges 1-7, party 6 at 100% HP, STEVEN_GUIDES_TO_CAVE_OF_ORIGIN set, SOOTOPOLIS_CITY_STATE=2. ⛔ (9,20) IS the warp tile back to Sootopolis (31,16) — any SOUTH step re-triggers it; leg 2b's first move is NORTH.
a6c28407f32dfd0415ee1b9433831cc5  post_wallace.ss1  PINNED  THE §Ch21 LEG-3 FIXTURE, captured 2026-08-27 by `--driver ch21cave` on FULL ACCEPTANCE. Probe-verified: OVERWORLD CAVE_OF_ORIGIN_B1F (9,14), badges 1-7, party 6 at 100%, SOOTOPOLIS_CITY_STATE=3, WALLACE_GOES_TO_SKY_PILLAR set, Wallace's object REMOVED (permanent). ✅ The pocket exit is MEASURED (2026-08-27, `--driver ch21pocket`): the walk out SUCCEEDS, §4.11's answer is the RESTING tile (31,17) NOT the warp target (31,16), and the pocket RE-SEALS behind the bot ⇒ ONE crossing per visit. ✅ **Leg 3 IS BUILT AND DRIVEN as of 2026-09-01** (`--driver ch21approach`, ACCEPTANCE: PASS, 14/14 readings, both fault arms run) and its output fixture is `post_skypillar_door.ss1`. ⛔ This row said "leg 3 is SPEC'D AND GATED but NOT BUILT" until then.
f6f8ab116b1bc18644286f51c2f202c6  post_skypillar_door.ss1  PINNED  THE §Ch21 LEG-3 OUTPUT FIXTURE, captured 2026-09-01 by `--driver ch21approach` on FULL ACCEPTANCE (all 14 readings, method_ok, premise_ok, control_refused). Probe-verified (probe_anchor_inventory): OVERWORLD SKY_PILLAR_ENTRANCE (6,16), badges 1-7, party 6. ⚠ HP is 629/694 (91%), NOT full — the 322-wp swim costs ~9 encounters and there is NO Poke Center between Sootopolis and the Sky Pillar, so leg 4 inherits a chipped party and must not assume otherwise. ⛔ (6,16) IS a SOUTH arrow warp back to ROUTE131, where the Sootopolis pocket has already RE-SEALED — never press or hold 'Down' from this fixture, and never use a helper that jolts the D-pad (walking.py's starve-jolt tries 'Down' FIRST). SOOTOPOLIS_CITY_STATE=3 and SKY_PILLAR_STATE=0, both UNCHANGED by leg 3 — state 4 is written by leg 4's Wallace door scene.
